## Page 22

4.1System Overview
FCIE is organised as four concentric layers — perception, state and knowledge, reasoning,
and delivery — connected through an event-driven backbone rather than direct point-to-
point calls, so that any layer can be re-trained, re-deployed, or swapped without a full-
system outage. The diagram below expands the original single-line pipeline sketch into its
true fan-out: the Knowledge Graph and Temporal Memory are shared substrates that both
the Causal Reasoning Engine and the Football LLM read from, and the API Gateway is the
single point of contact for every downstream client.
