4.2Perception & State Modules
① Video Ingestion Pipeline PERCEPTION
PURPOSE Turn a raw broadcast or fixed tactical-camera feed into a calibrated, timestamp-
aligned frame stream every downstream module can trust.
RESPONSIBILITIES Ingest upload or live stream; extract frames at target FPS; camera calibration and
pitch-plane homography; multi-camera timestamp sync.
INPUTS Video file or RTMP/HLS stream; optional camera-position metadata.
OUTPUTS Calibrated frame stream with per-frame pitch-coordinate homography matrix and
timestamp.
INTERNAL AL‐
GORITHMS
Homography estimation from pitch-line detection; keyframe-based re-calibration for
camera pans/zooms; FFmpeg-based decode.
DEPENDENCIES FFmpeg, OpenCV; object storage (raw footage retention).
FAILURE MODES Poor calibration under rapid camera pans; dropped frames on unstable live streams;
broadcast cuts (replays, adverts) polluting the timeline.
SCALABILITY Embarrassingly parallel across matches; GPU-accelerated decode for live multi-match
ingestion.
FUTURE IM‐
PROVEMENTS
Multi-camera fusion for single-feed occlusion recovery; automatic broadcast-cut
detection to mask non-play segments.
PART IV — SOFTWARE ARCHITECTURE FOOTBALL CAUSAL INTELLIGENCE ENGINE
