## Page 24

② Computer Vision Layer PERCEPTION
PURPOSE Convert pixels into the raw ingredients of St: who is where, moving how, facing
which way.
RESPONSIBILITIES Player/referee/ball detection; multi-object tracking with re-identification across
occlusion; pose estimation; (future) jersey-number OCR.
INPUTS Calibrated frame stream from Module ①.
OUTPUTS Per-frame records: {frame, player_id, x, y, velocity, orientation, ball_position, confid‐
ence}.
INTERNAL AL‐
GORITHMS
YOLOv11/RT-DETR for detection; ByteTrack or StrongSORT for tracking-by-detection;
MediaPipe/HRNet-family for pose.
DEPENDENCIES GPU inference cluster (Module ⑯); calibration output from Module ①.
FAILURE MODES Identity switches during pile-ups and goal celebrations; ball occlusion during head‐
ers/tackles; far-side player miniaturisation reducing detection confidence.
SCALABILITY Batched GPU inference; tracker state is per-match and horizontally shardable across
concurrent matches.
FUTURE IM‐
PROVEMENTS
Learned re-identification embeddings robust to kit changes (goalkeepers, second-half
kit swaps); jersey-number recognition to remove manual ID mapping.
