## Page 25

③ World State Builder PERCEPTION
PURPOSE Assemble raw per-frame CV output into the structured St tuple defined in Part II.
RESPONSIBILITIES Coordinate normalisation to a standard pitch frame; velocity/acceleration smoothing;
team-side and formation-label assignment; context merge (score, clock, cards).
INPUTS CV layer output; match metadata feed (score, substitutions, officials).
OUTPUTS Time-indexed St records, persisted to the time-series store and streamed to Modules
④–⑥.
INTERNAL AL‐
GORITHMS
Kalman/particle-filter smoothing of noisy tracks; rule-based team/side assignment
with learned fallback.
DEPENDENCIES Time-series database (Module ⑮); Module ② output stream.
FAILURE MODES Smoothing over-correction during genuine sharp accelerations (sprints, sliding
tackles); metadata-feed lag desynchronising score/clock from tracking.
SCALABILITY Streaming (Kafka-style) construction enables near-real-time St for live matches, not
just post-hoc batch.
FUTURE IM‐
PROVEMENTS
Uncertainty-aware state (confidence intervals on position, not point estimates)
propagated into every downstream layer .
