④ Spatial Intelligence Engine UNDERSTANDING
PURPOSE Compute the pitch-control field pteam(x,y,t) and everything derived from it (Section
2.7).
RESPONSIBILITIES Dynamic Voronoi/probabilistic control regions; dangerous-space scoring; numerical-
overload detection; passing-lane enumeration and interception-risk.
INPUTS St stream from Module ③.
OUTPUTS Πt (pressure field), Λt (passing lanes), occupancy/control grids at configurable resolu‐
tion.
INTERNAL AL‐
GORITHMS
Probabilistic pitch-control models conditioned on velocity and reaction time; graph-
based occupancy reasoning for overload counts.
DEPENDENCIES GPU or vectorised CPU grid computation; Module ③.
FAILURE MODES Grid resolution trade-offs (coarse grids miss tight overloads; fine grids are compute-
heavy at scale); reaction-time priors that don't generalise across leagues/age groups.
SCALABILITY Per-frame computation is independent and GPU-vectorisable across the whole pitch
grid simultaneously.
FUTURE IM‐
PROVEMENTS
Player-specific reaction and top-speed priors learned from historical tracking rather
than league-wide constants.
