⑤ Tactical Understanding UNDERSTANDING
PURPOSE Produce the tactical abstraction τt = φ(St) defined in Section 2.3.
RESPONSIBILITIES Phase classification (build-up, progression, transition, defensive recovery); press-
trigger and block-height recognition; overload and rest-defence scoring.
INPUTS St, Πt, Λt from Modules ③–④.
OUTPUTS τt tactical-state stream; phase-change events for Module ⑥.
INTERNAL AL‐
GORITHMS
Temporal transformers / TCNs over windows of St; weak supervision from coach-
provided phase tags for alignment.
DEPENDENCIES Modules ③–④; a labelled phase dataset for supervision/fine-tuning.
FAILURE MODES Ambiguous phase boundaries (build-up sliding into progression has no hard edge);
label scarcity for rarer phases (rest-defence in transition).
SCALABILITY Windowed inference batches cheaply; model size is the main lever on latency for live
use.
FUTURE IM‐
PROVEMENTS
Self-supervised pre-training on unlabelled footage (Part V, §5.9) to reduce
dependence on scarce phase labels.
