⑥ T emporal Memory Layer UNDERSTANDING
PURPOSE Carry the compressed memory state Mt that makes non-Markovian transitions
(Section 2.4) tractable.
RESPONSIBILITIES Long-range dependency storage; match-level "what both teams have learned so far"
summarisation; retrieval of relevant historical state for the Causal Reasoning Engine.
INPUTS τt stream; phase-change events from Module ⑤.
OUTPUTS Mt memory embeddings; retrievable historical-state index.
INTERNAL AL‐
GORITHMS
Transformer memory / recurrent state-space models; vector index for similarity
retrieval over past tactical states.
DEPENDENCIES Vector database (Module ⑮); Module ⑤ output.
FAILURE MODES Memory dilution over very long matches (extra time); irrelevant-history retrieval
polluting causal search.
SCALABILITY Memory embeddings are fixed-size regardless of match length; retrieval scales with
vector-index size, not raw frame count.
FUTURE IM‐
PROVEMENTS
Season-level memory spanning multiple matches, for "this is the third time this team
has been exposed by the same trap" reasoning.
