4.3Reasoning & Knowledge Modules
⑦ Football Knowledge Graph REASONING
PURPOSE Persist every entity and relationship the reasoning and language layers need to
query — the shared substrate of the system. Full schema in Part VIII.
RESPONSIBILITIES Ingest entities (players, teams, spaces, passes, tactical states) and relationships (cre‐
ated, blocked, occupied, pressed, supported, enabled) with temporal validity.
INPUTS τt, Mt, and Domino Moment records from Modules ⑤, ⑥, ⑧.
OUTPUTS Queryable graph (Cypher); subgraph retrieval for RAG (Module ⑩).
INTERNAL AL‐
GORITHMS
Incremental graph construction; temporal edge versioning; graph embeddings for
approximate/semantic queries.
DEPENDENCIES Neo4j (or equivalent property graph store); ingestion queue from upstream modules.
FAILURE MODES Schema drift as new edge types are added ad hoc; write contention during high-
frequency live-match ingestion.
SCALABILITY Read replicas for dashboard/LLM query load; write path sharded by match.
FUTURE IM‐
PROVEMENTS
Cross-match, cross-season graph federation for opponent scouting queries that span
a whole competition.
