15.1Glossary
Domino Moment
The earliest state transition with high, min‐
imal  causal  influence  on  a  downstream
outcome (§2.5, §6.1).
Influence
Estimated causal effect size of a decision
on an outcome, I(vi) (§6.2).
Importance
Influence  combined  with  rarity  and  re‐
versibility; the coach-facing ranking score
(§6.3).
World State (St)
The full low-level match state tuple at time
t (§2.2).
Tactical State (τt)
Compressed, coach-legible abstraction of St
(§2.3).
Pitch Control
Probability  field  over  who  reaches  each
pitch location first (§2.7).
Tactical Entropy
Shannon entropy over the outcome/control
distribution; a measure of match disorder
(§2.11).
Cognitive Load
Proxy for decision difficulty facing a player
at a given instant (§2.10).
Decision Chain
Directed  graph  of  sequential  decision
points within a possession (§2.12).
Causal Chain
A Decision Chain with edges weighted by
estimated causal influence (§2.13).
Counterfactual
The estimated alternative outcome under a
different  action  at  a  decision  point  (Part
VII).
Structural Causal Model (SCM)
Pearl-style  formalism  relating  variables
through  causal,  not  merely  correlational,
structure.
do(·)
The  intervention  operator:  "set  this  vari‐
able  by  intervention,"  not  "condition  on
observing this value."
Match Narrative
Ranked  Domino  Moments  strung  into  a
causally-ordered  account  of  how  an
outcome arose (§2.14).
Hidden Tactical Structure
Latent  variable  Zt capturing  unobserved
coaching intent (§2.15).
Knowledge Graph
The temporal property graph storing entit‐
ies and relationships across a match (Part
VIII).
RAG
Retrieval-Augmented  Generation  —
grounding  LLM  output  in  retrieved  evid‐
ence  rather  than  parametric  memory
alone.
World Model
A learned model of state-transition dynam‐
ics used to simulate counterfactual rollouts
(§5.6).
GNN
PART XV — APPENDICES FOOTBALL CAUSAL INTELLIGENCE ENGINE
75

## Page 76

Graph Neural Network — message-passing
model  over  player-interaction  graphs
(§5.3).
Expected Threat (xT)
Established possession-value metric estim‐
ating  scoring  probability  from  ball  loca‐
tion.
VAEP
Established  action-valuation  framework
crediting  individual  actions  by  predicted
probability shift.
PPDA
Passes-per-defensive-action  —  an  estab‐
lished aggregate pressing-intensity metric.
Confounding
A  third  variable  influencing  both  a  de‐
cision  and  its  outcome,  biasing  naive
causal estimates (§1.4).
Non‐stationarity
Drift in causal relationships over time as
tactics and opponents adapt (§14.3).
Sim‐to‐real gap
Divergence between a learned simulator's
behaviour  and  true  real-world  dynamics
(§14.5).
Contrastive Learning
Representation-learning  objective  pulling
similar  examples  together  and  dissimilar
ones apart in embedding space (§5.8).
